DescriptionPOSITION SUMMARYReporting to Senior Management and Managers of both internal and external Client Services teams, the Senior Manager / Director, Client Service, is responsible for executing strategies with a strong client-focused orientation with an emphasis on identifying and mitigating new Business Development risks.
Client Service provides ongoing client-oriented activities, including:
-Developing and managing Client Contracts;
-Review policies/industry compliance;
-Monitor, evaluate and report performance to Internal & External clients (as well as outside agencies).
Risk Manager is required to conduct, coordinate and participate in the analysis (both substantive and written), and evaluation (qualitative and quantitive) of business transactions and projects, as well as, provide consults to clients, regulators and other stakeholder(s). The ability and demonstrated expertise in the various fields is required, especially IT-related risks.
Principal Responsibilities include, but are not limited to,
Providing review and update on regulatory and product development related documents;
Performing due diligence on contracts and products with a strong understanding of their design requirements, legal structures
